Negative control for the FLAG-IS-THE-ICON-CELL law (`R6-34`).

Reads the row's flag off the BADGES cell instead of the icon cell, so the row
treatment answers to a field the star does not draw: the record whose star is
filled and the record the surface tints are no longer the same one. This is the
failure the deleted `marker` channel could always produce — a second declaration
of which boolean means special — reintroduced by pointing the derivation at the
wrong cell.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the list-surface marked-row spec — the row drawn with the filled star is
the row carrying the marked treatment, in the table and in card view alike.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/modules/scenarios/runtime/components/surfaces/ListSurface.vue
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@
  */
 function isMarked(row: ListRow): boolean {
   return some(
-    filter(columnElements.value, { type: "TableCellIcon" }),
+    filter(columnElements.value, { type: "TableCellBadges" }),
     element => !!resolveScope(row, element.scope)
   );
 }
